0..74 Comment "//! The block operations of `boot-core` over `Ptr.Eff`: a copy between two"
75..153 Comment "//! ranges that share no byte, a move between two ranges that can share bytes,"
154..194 Comment "//! a fill, and the order of two ranges."
195..198 Comment "//!"
199..274 Comment "//! `copy`, `move_bytes`, `fill` and `compare` give the answers of the Rust"
275..354 Comment "//! functions of `crates/boot-core/src/block.rs`. They name no model of memory:"
355..430 Comment "//! the scope that handles `Ptr.Eff` chooses one. Each reads and writes one"
431..507 Comment "//! byte at a time with `load8` and `store8`, and it touches no byte outside"
508..587 Comment "//! its ranges. An empty range can have any address, and no operation reads it."
588..667 Comment "//! Each operation descends on the length of a range, as `ranges.gandr` states."
668..671 Comment "//!"
672..749 Comment "//! The `runs` items run the cases of `crates/boot-core/tests/block.rs` under"
750..828 Comment "//! `Extent`. A range that ends at the end of a page in the Rust tests ends at"
829..899 Comment "//! the end of the extent here, so an access past it ends the run with"
900..978 Comment "//! `Outside`. An empty range at the address 0 is the null address of the Rust"
979..1034 Comment "//! tests: an access there ends the run with `Outside`."
1035..1038 Comment "//!"
1039..1089 Comment "//! - see: `ranges.gandr` — `Range` and `Length`"
1090..1164 Comment "//! - see: `../../../library/std/src/ptr.gandr` — `Ptr.Eff` and `Extent`"
1165..1239 Comment "//! - see: `../../../crates/boot-core/src/block.rs` — the Rust functions"
1241..1278 Comment "// The bytes of a memory of `Extent`."
